WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.323
Hi, I'm Rowan!

00:00:02.323 --> 00:00:05.421
Adapt-1 Machina teaches a simulated arm with no critic.

00:00:05.421 --> 00:00:07.486
So what does the critic's job?

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:11.876
The simulator is the critic.

00:00:11.876 --> 00:00:15.692
Propose a whole sequence of commands, run it, grade the outcome,

00:00:15.692 --> 00:00:17.080
and revise earlier attempts.

00:00:18.692 --> 00:00:20.165
An attempt is one matrix.

00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:21.638
Each row is a command.

00:00:22.058 --> 00:00:23.395
Three numbers place the tool,

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:25.716
three turn it,

00:00:27.762 --> 00:00:29.083
and one sets the gripper.

00:00:30.031 --> 00:00:34.180
Up to twenty rows, a hundred and forty numbers, committed before the arm moves.

00:00:35.692 --> 00:00:40.026
Propose the whole matrix at once: one decision per attempt, not per step.

00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:42.177
Run it in the simulator.

00:00:42.177 --> 00:00:43.909
Nothing estimates its value first.

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:49.007
Hand-written detectors grade it: contact, lift, transfer above the receptacle, and a

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:50.566
placement that stays put.

00:00:50.986 --> 00:00:55.845
Then revise a recorded attempt: keep its opening, and change a few indexed numbers.

00:00:57.342 --> 00:00:59.643
Beyond search, one part is learned.

00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:02.712
It reads the starting observation through quadratic features.

00:01:03.132 --> 00:01:06.383
It outputs a bounded correction, from weights that start at zero.

00:01:06.803 --> 00:01:10.094
The correction is added to the sequence the search found, and clipped

00:01:10.094 --> 00:01:11.191
to the allowed range.

00:01:12.592 --> 00:01:17.018
Feed the correction another case's observation, and it does worse than none

00:01:17.018 --> 00:01:18.862
at all: sixty-two against eighty-five.

00:01:18.862 --> 00:01:21.074
So it really reads the observation.

00:01:22.592 --> 00:01:27.216
On three hundred and eighty-four unseen layouts, placements rose six point two

00:01:27.216 --> 00:01:29.528
five points: seventy gained, forty-six broken.

00:01:29.528 --> 00:01:32.610
The interval's low end is under one point.

00:01:34.142 --> 00:01:38.081
No critic doesn't mean no cost: the simulator does the critic's job,

00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:40.050
one executed attempt at a time.

00:01:42.192 --> 00:01:46.156
To recap: propose a matrix, let the simulator grade it, edit, and

00:01:46.156 --> 00:01:47.477
learn one small correction.

00:01:47.897 --> 00:01:49.924
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:49.924 --> 00:01:50.503
I'm Rowan.

00:01:50.503 --> 00:01:50.792
Bye!
